iterations.reply:
The build failed because the top-level `use`, `import`, and `export` lines in `wit/world.wit` are not valid outside a world, and the world's own declarations were duplicated. The Rust side was fine apart from that. I've fixed the world file and kept the component body as it was.

I did not add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and the spec makes that the node's entire authority. Importing an interface the host does not grant would fail at instantiation. The fetch would also send untrusted feed text into an outbound URL. Once the graph's `with` clause lists `http-client` and the enrichment design is settled, the import can be added.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

